  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nSouthwesterly winds today will allow temperatures to warm \nconsiderably. Afternoon readings will be in the 80s for all but\nthe higher elevations. \n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\n\nA cold front will push southward through the region on Friday, \nbringing showers and thunderstorms. Models show the front \nstalling south of the region Friday night. The area will remain\nclose enough to the front however, that some rain or drizzle\nwill remain possible into Saturday, more likely over southern \nWest Virginia and southwest Virginia. \n\nAn upper level wave will move across the area on Sunday,\nenhancing the chances of precipitation. Once again, this will \nbe more likely over southern West Virginia and southwest \nVirginia. This system will also push the cold front further\nsouth, leaving dry weather for the beginning of the next work\nweek.",
